  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the supplied task/tooling notes and workspace first, then build the app and run the requested route, browser, durability, concurrency, and load checks. I’ll preserve the supplied instructions and keep all project writes inside the workspace.",
    "The workspace is empty apart from the task notes. I’ve set up a dependency-free Python/SQLite backend with tenant-scoped records and serialized write transactions; next I’m adding the responsive workflow UI, integration coverage, and repeatable browser/load exercises.",
    "The first integration run did not reach the health route, so I’m diagnosing startup before expanding verification. The code compiles; I’ll capture the server’s startup error, correct it, and rerun the full route suite.",
    "The server startup issue was a collision with `BaseHTTPRequestHandler.handle`; it’s fixed, and the integration suite now passes across auth, isolation, atomic stock reservation, retries, returns, and restart durability. I’m adding the browser and load scripts next so the requested UI workflow and performance numbers can be captured reproducibly.",
    "The browser workflow now completes order creation through full return and confirms logout. Its narrow-screen check found a 132px horizontal overflow in the orders view; I’m locating the element that expands the layout and will fix that before recording the final browser evidence.",
    "The mobile overflow came from grid children honoring their tables’ intrinsic minimum widths. I constrained the card tracks and kept the tables scrollable inside their panels. Browser automation now passes the full operator flow, confirms the viewer has no write controls, checks inventory and orders at 390px, and reports no browser errors. Next I’m capturing the mixed read/write load results and writing the runbook/architecture notes.",
    "The integration suite now also checks concurrent identical retries and confirms failed reservation attempts leave audit history unchanged. The clean-store load run completed 1,000 requests with zero errors; I’m doing the final browser pass and cleanup, then I’ll report the evidence and any limits.",
    "DepotFlow is implemented as a locally runnable Python/SQLite app with a responsive UI, tenant-scoped authorization, atomic stock and order transitions, durable idempotency, audit history, integration tests, and a load generator.\n\n**Verification passed:** the route and restart suite passed; the browser workflow covered order creation through full return and viewer access at 390px, with no browser errors or page overflow. The 1,000-request, 16-worker load run recorded **2,536.96 requests/s and 0 errors**; read p50/p95 was 0.79/4.13 ms and write p50/p95 was 1.75/126.02 ms.\n\n- [Setup, commands, results, and limits](<<CELL>/workspace/README.md>)\n- [Architecture and invariants](<<CELL>/workspace/architecture.md>)\n- [Executable run script](<<CELL>/workspace/run.sh>)\n- [Integration test output](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/api-tests.txt>), [browser run and screenshots](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/browser-run.json>), and [load results](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/load-results.json>)\n\nThe documented limits are a local, single-process deployment, SQLite’s serialized writes, and demo sessions without expiration."
  ],
  "final": "DepotFlow is implemented as a locally runnable Python/SQLite app with a responsive UI, tenant-scoped authorization, atomic stock and order transitions, durable idempotency, audit history, integration tests, and a load generator.\n\n**Verification passed:** the route and restart suite passed; the browser workflow covered order creation through full return and viewer access at 390px, with no browser errors or page overflow. The 1,000-request, 16-worker load run recorded **2,536.96 requests/s and 0 errors**; read p50/p95 was 0.79/4.13 ms and write p50/p95 was 1.75/126.02 ms.\n\n- [Setup, commands, results, and limits](<<CELL>/workspace/README.md>)\n- [Architecture and invariants](<<CELL>/workspace/architecture.md>)\n- [Executable run script](<<CELL>/workspace/run.sh>)\n- [Integration test output](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/api-tests.txt>), [browser run and screenshots](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/browser-run.json>), and [load results](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/load-results.json>)\n\nThe documented limits are a local, single-process deployment, SQLite’s serialized writes, and demo sessions without expiration.",
